
==========================================================================
  INSTANTIATED QSWITCH E2E DEMO (Linear DSL)
==========================================================================

Demonstrating compositional use of abstract QSwitch

All QSwitch instances use proper Linear DSL:
  dist_l ; omap0 left_branch right_branch ; undist_l


==========================================================================
  PART 1: Basic QSwitch Instantiations
==========================================================================

QSwitch[H, S]:
  ctrl=0 → H(S(x)) = S ; H
  ctrl=1 → S(H(x)) = H ; S

QSwitch[H, S]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[X, Z] (Pauli gates):
  ctrl=0 → X(Z(x)) = Z ; X
  ctrl=1 → Z(X(x)) = X ; Z

QSwitch[X, Z]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[H, Y]:
  ctrl=0 → H(Y(x)) = Y ; H
  ctrl=1 → Y(H(x)) = H ; Y

QSwitch[H, Y]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CY q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CY q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  PART 2: Composed QSwitch Applications
==========================================================================

Composing multiple QSwitch applications demonstrates:
  - The same control qubit sequences multiple operations
  - Each QSwitch contributes gates coherently
  - Types ensure composition is valid

QSwitch[H,S] ; QSwitch[X,Z]:
  Type: (Bool ⊗ Q) → (Bool ⊗ Q) → (Bool ⊗ Q)

Composed:
2 qubits, 12 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[H,S] ; QSwitch[X,Z] ; QSwitch[H,Y]:

Triple composed:
2 qubits, 18 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CY q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CY q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  PART 3: Self-Inverse QSwitch (f = g)
==========================================================================

When f = g, QSwitch[f, f] applies f;f in both branches:
  - Both orderings are the same!
  - This is a uniform operation regardless of control state

For involutive f (f;f = id), this becomes identity on Q!


QSwitch[H, H]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[S, S]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[X, X]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  PART 4: QSwitch with Parameterized Rotations
==========================================================================

QSwitch can be parameterized with any Q → Q morphism.
Using Rz rotations:


QSwitch[Rz(π/4), Rz(π/8)]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

QSwitch[Rz(π/4), Rz(-π/4)]:
2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  PART 5: Verify Structural Isomorphisms
==========================================================================

Verifying that dist_l and undist_l are proper inverses:

dist_l one one q:
  {"node": "DistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}

undist_l one one q:
  {"node": "UndistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}

dist_l ; undist_l (should be identity):

Roundtrip:
2 qubits, 0 gates
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

Demonstrated compositional use of abstract QSwitch:

1. BASIC INSTANTIATION
   qswitch gate_h gate_s - creates QSwitch for any gate pair

2. SEQUENTIAL COMPOSITION
   seq0 qswitch1 qswitch2 - chains multiple QSwitch ops
   Types ensure composition is valid

3. PARAMETERIZED CONSTRUCTION
   qswitch (gate_rz theta) (gate_rz phi) - factory function

4. SELF-INVERSE CASE
   qswitch gate_h gate_h - when both gates are the same

5. STRUCTURAL ISOMORPHISMS
   dist_l ; undist_l = id  (verified by compilation)

Key insight: QSwitch is a FIRST-CLASS COMBINATOR in the Linear DSL
  - Defined using proper structural isomorphisms
  - GADT-enforced linearity
  - Composes naturally with type safety
  - No Bridge term hacking!


